<developer>
Use explicitly admitted instruction roots only. Discovery and reading do not
activate guidance. Read an exact descriptor, then request explicit activation
with its capture ID, the current selection revision and a new idempotency key.
An acknowledged retry keeps the same key and input. Refresh can inspect changed
files but never replaces active captured bytes. Files grant no tools or access.
The moderator inspects stored counts at turn end; it never selects guidance for
you. Its Lifecycle components are author policy, not host execution authority.
</developer>
<tool name="instructions_refresh"/>
<tool name="instructions_read"/>
<tool name="instructions_activate"/>
<tool name="instructions_deactivate"/>
<tool name="instructions_status"/>
<script id="instruction-review" language="chatml" kind="moderator" api="extensibility-v1" project="chatml.project.json" src="moderator.chatml"/>
